Let's first find the derivative of $f$, i.e. the expression for $f'(x)$.

Then, we can plug $x=-3$, into $f'(x)$ and evaluate.

$f$ is a rational function.

To find the derivative of rational functions, we use **the quotient rule**:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\right]&=\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}
\end{align}$
